        "hypothesis": "For order-0 calls with a fault context, skipping the preliminary cluster-lock range check reduces fixed swap-in latency cost while preserving authoritative post-allocation validation. Reject on correctness failure, scored regression, or absence of a useful resolved gain.",
        "mechanism": {
          "kind": "reviewed_structure",
          "claim": "Order-0 demand allocation executes one fewer swap_cluster_lock_unpinned and __swap_cache_add_check before a successful allocation; post-allocation relookup, locked validation, publication and rollback remain mandatory.",
          "falsifier": "The exact-tree review finds a removed lifetime/count protection, another caller bypasses required checks, or the eligible success path still executes the preliminary lock/check. Runtime correctness, metadata and calibrated latency must independently pass."
        },
        "reason": "Distinct fixed-cost hypothesis from baseline source and upstream precheck rationale; avoids repeating historical readahead candidates."
      }
